title: Authorizations › Queue › Bands and ranking
route: /authorizations
intro: How open requests are split into three bands, how they are ranked inside a band by money and time, and how a band opens, closes and shows more.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: which band a request sits in is fixed in the seed data. Moving the demo clock changes the due text on each tile ('in 5 h', 'now') but never moves a request to another band.
---
screen q "Queue\nPriority bands, most urgent first"
process b1 "Each open request sits in exactly one band"

group gB "The three bands, in this order"
  process bn "**Act now**\nRed dot, tiles tinted red"
  process bd "**Due within 24 hours**\nAmber dot"
  process bw "**Due this week**\nSage dot"
endgroup

decision dE "Does the band have any request after filters?"
process hide "The band card is left out"
screen bc "Band card\n'Act now (5 requests)'\nName, count, chevron"

process r1 "Inside a band, requests waiting on a person come first\nPreparing, Ready to sign, Denial route, or Needs your input"
process r2 "Then money at risk times a time weight, biggest first"
process wt "Time weight by time left\nunder 6 h ×3 · under 24 h ×2 · under 3 days ×1.5 · later ×1"
doc ex "Example in Act now\nR-1042 ($22.4K, due in 5 h) ranks above R-0912 (payer already reviewing)"

click hd "Click the band header"
decision dC "Is the band open now?"
process col "Tiles are hidden\nChevron turns sideways"
process exp "Tiles are shown\nChevron points down"
store keep "Open or closed is remembered for each band\nuntil the demo data is reset"

decision dM "More than five requests in the band?"
process all5 "All requests are shown"
process top5 "Top five are shown\nButton under them: 'Show 9 more'"
click sm "Click 'Show 9 more'"
process allm "Every request is shown\nButton now reads 'Show fewer'"
click sf "Click 'Show fewer'"
process back "Back to the top five"

goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Queue › Read and open a request tile"

q --> b1
b1 --> bn & bd & bw
bn --> dE
bd --> dE
bw --> dE
dE -->|No| hide
dE -->|Yes| bc
bc --> r1 --> r2 --> wt
r2 -.-> ex
bc --> hd --> dC
dC -->|Yes| col --> keep
dC -->|No| exp --> keep
bc --> dM
dM -->|No| all5
dM -->|Yes| top5 --> sm --> allm --> sf --> back
top5 --> g1
